---@class planetscale.CreateBranchRequest
---@field organization string The name of the organization the branch belongs to
---@field database string The name of the database the branch belongs to
---@field name string The name of the branch to create
---@field deletion_protected? boolean Whether deletion protection is enabled for the branch
---@field parent_branch? string The name of the parent branch. Defaults to the database's default branch if not provided.
---@field backup_id? string If provided, restores the backup's schema and data to the new branch. Must have `restore_production_branch_backup(s)` or `restore_backup(s)` access to do this.
---@field region? string The region to create the branch in. If not provided, the branch will be created in the default region for its database.
---@field restore_point? string Restore from a point-in-time recovery timestamp (e.g. 2023-01-01T00:00:00Z). Available only for PostgreSQL databases.
---@field replicas? number For PostgreSQL backup restores and point-in-time recovery, the number of additional replicas from 0 to 8, subject to the target cluster size. 0 creates a single-node branch. If omitted, the target cluster size's minimum is used.
---@field seed_data? planetscale.CreateBranchRequestSeedData|string If provided, restores the last successful backup's schema and data to the new branch. Must have `restore_production_branch_backup(s)` or `restore_backup(s)` access to do this, in addition to Data Branching™ being enabled for the branch.
---@field cluster_size? string The database cluster size. Required if a backup_id is provided (unless keyspace_cluster_sizes covers every keyspace), optional otherwise. Options: PS_10, PS_20, PS_40, ..., PS_2800
---@field keyspace_cluster_sizes? planetscale.CreateBranchRequestKeyspaceClusterSizesList For MySQL backup restores, per-keyspace cluster sizes. Each entry is { "keyspace_name": "main", "cluster_size": "PS_40" }. When provided, each restored keyspace must have a size here or via cluster_size.
---@field configuration_profile_sizes? planetscale.CreateBranchRequestConfigurationProfileSizesList For Neki backup restores, per-configuration-profile cluster size and replica count. Each entry is { "name": "default", "cluster_size": "PS_40", "replicas": 2 }. Omitted profiles inherit the source size and replica count.
---@field router_sizes? planetscale.CreateBranchRequestRouterSizesList For Neki backup restores, per-router size and replica count. Each entry is { "name": "default", "router_size": "NKR_20", "replicas_per_cell": 1 }. Omitted routers inherit the source size and replica count.
---@field storage? planetscale.CreateBranchRequestStorage
---@field major_version? string For PostgreSQL and Neki databases, the PostgreSQL major version to use for the branch. Defaults to the major version of the parent branch if it exists or the database's default branch major version. Ignored for branches restored from backups.
---@field create_database_if_missing? boolean Create a new database for the branch if the database does not exist. Defaults to false.
---@field kind? planetscale.CreateBranchRequestKind|string The kind of branch to create. Required when create_database_if_missing is set.

---For Neki backup restores, per-configuration-profile cluster size and replica count. Each entry is { "name": "default", "cluster_size": "PS_40", "replicas": 2 }. Omitted profiles inherit the source size and replica count.
---@alias planetscale.CreateBranchRequestConfigurationProfileSizesList string[]

---For MySQL backup restores, per-keyspace cluster sizes. Each entry is { "keyspace_name": "main", "cluster_size": "PS_40" }. When provided, each restored keyspace must have a size here or via cluster_size.
---@alias planetscale.CreateBranchRequestKeyspaceClusterSizesList string[]

---The kind of branch to create. Required when create_database_if_missing is set.
---@alias planetscale.CreateBranchRequestKind "mysql"|"postgresql"|"neki"

---For Neki backup restores, per-router size and replica count. Each entry is { "name": "default", "router_size": "NKR_20", "replicas_per_cell": 1 }. Omitted routers inherit the source size and replica count.
---@alias planetscale.CreateBranchRequestRouterSizesList string[]

---If provided, restores the last successful backup's schema and data to the new branch. Must have `restore_production_branch_backup(s)` or `restore_backup(s)` access to do this, in addition to Data Branching™ being enabled for the branch.
